     {
      "t": "p",
      "v": [
       {
        "t": "text",
        "v": "The Admin API needs an "
       },
       {
        "t": "code",
        "v": "sk-ant-admin..."
       },
       {
        "t": "text",
        "v": " key, which only admins can provision, or an OAuth token with the "
       },
       {
        "t": "code",
        "v": "org:admin"
       },
       {
        "t": "text",
        "v": " scope. Workspace roles are Workspace User, Limited Developer, Developer, Admin, and Billing (inherited from the org billing role). Org admins automatically get Workspace Admin everywhere. [16][17]"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "t": "p",
      "v": [
       {
        "t": "text",
        "v": "A "
       },
       {
        "t": "strong",
        "v": "Claude Code workspace"
       },
       {
        "t": "text",
        "v": " is created automatically the first time a member signs in to Claude Code with a Console account. Claude Code mints a per-user key in it; you cannot create keys there manually. It is the only workspace that supports per-user monthly spend limits, and archiving it disables Claude Code sign-in for the whole org. On Teams and Enterprise, usage draws instead from a per-seat allowance on rolling five-hour and weekly windows, sized by Standard or Premium seat tier, with usage credits and spend limits set in the claude.ai admin console. [17][18]"
       }
      ]
     }
